    {
      "id": "f6c7e426-f3a4-493c-abaa-8e3c38912f87",
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        48,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 536,
        "height": 992,
        "content": "# Score call audio with Tyto and flag risky calls\n\n## Who's it for\n\nVoice AI and conversational AI engineers, and contact-center ops teams, who push audio through a voice stack (VAD, turn-taking, STT, speech-to-speech) and need to catch calls likely to fail before anyone listens.\n\n## What it does\n\nEvery call is scored by ai-coustics Tyto, which returns a risk_score from 0 to 1, a band, and the main degradation cause: noise, speaker reverb, interfering speech, background media speech, or packet loss. Risky calls (risk_score above 0.60) are flagged with the score and the cause. Clean calls are logged. The workflow responds with the scored JSON so you can store or chain it.\n\n## How to set up\n\nTyto runs on the AIC SDK on CPU, on-prem, so it has no public endpoint. Run the small HTTP wrapper (linked in the setup notes) on a machine with the Tyto SDK and your AIC license key. Edit api_base_url in the Set node to point at it. Add your Slack credential, or swap Slack for Notion or Sheets.\n\n## Requirements\n\nn8n, a running Tyto wrapper, an AIC license key (free self-service at developers.ai-coustics.com), and a destination credential such as Slack, Notion, or Google Sheets.\n\n## How to customize\n\nTune the risky threshold, add a warn tier for 0.35 to 0.60, or group flagged calls by cause to separate systemic issues from one-offs.\n\nSelf-hosted only: needs the Tyto HTTP wrapper (tyto_score_api.py) running on-prem."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9d7b3220-010f-4c8f-ab4d-43350012d3a7",
      "name": "Note: configure and score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        848,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 360,
        "height": 280,
        "content": "### 1. Configure and score\n\nEdit **api_base_url** in the Set node to point at your Tyto wrapper (use http://127.0.0.1:8000 for local).\n\nThe Set node also pulls audio_url and call_id from the webhook body. The HTTP node sends them to Tyto and returns risk_score, band, and the main cause."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d7074321-5484-438c-b16e-1eadc805f553",
      "name": "Note: route",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1456,
        384
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 344,
        "height": 264,
        "content": "### 2. Route\n\nRisky calls (band = bad, risk_score above 0.60) fire the Slack alert.\n\nEverything else is logged as OK.\n\nSwap Slack for Notion, Sheets, or a ticket by replacing that one node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
